## Prometheus exposition-format worked example

`src/root.zig`'s test `"conformance: the checker accepts Prometheus's own
published exposition-format example"` embeds (`prom_golden_example`) a
verbatim excerpt of the worked example published at
https://prometheus.io/docs/instrumenting/exposition_formats/, fetched
2026-08-01. The Prometheus documentation site states its content is
available under the Apache License 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0), copyright The Linux Foundation
/ Prometheus Authors.

The excerpt deliberately omits the page's "UTF-8 metric and label names"
example line and the closing "summary" section: those exercise format
extensions/metric kinds (bare-brace UTF-8 metric names; the `summary` type
with `quantile` labels) that this module's writer never emits and that the
accompanying grammar checker (`validateExpositionText`) does not need to
accept to do its job here.

Purpose: this text is used purely as a frozen, offline ANCHOR for a hand-
written exposition-format grammar checker — proving the checker accepts
real, externally-authored conformant text, not merely this module's own
output shape (see the governing rule discussion in `src/root.zig`). No
Prometheus/OpenMetrics source code of any kind is used, ported, or
consulted; only this one short block of example prose/text.
